# 0006. Install layout: shipped files replaced, user settings never touched

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-05

Files the repo ships are replaced on every `make install`; the two files the user edits live in
`/etc/archminimal-greeter` and are never overwritten.

## Technical details
- **Replaced on install**: `/usr/share/archminimal-greeter/` (QML, `list-sessions.sh`, wallpaper,
  greeter-only `hyprland.lua`), `/usr/local/bin/archminimal-greeter`, the tmpfiles entry.
- **Kept**: `/etc/archminimal-greeter/config.json` (installed only if missing; colours, header text,
  remember user, default session, power buttons, glitch, scanlines, login position, primary screen)
  and `/etc/archminimal-greeter/local.lua` (keyboard layout, monitors for the login screen), loaded
  last by the greeter's `hyprland.lua` with `pcall(dofile, …)`; a real error is re-raised.
- **Migration**: older versions copied `hyprland.lua` to `/etc` and never updated it; install moves it
  to `hyprland.lua.unused`. Every installed path is named `archminimal-greeter`; renaming one needs a
  migration in `make install`.
- **Install check**: ends with `✓ installed` only if the new launcher and config are in place;
  `make status` says `launcher: up to date` or `OUTDATED`.
- **Preview**: `make preview` runs the greeter in a window with the repo's `config/config.json`
  (no login, no power actions).
- **Consequences**: `git pull && sudo make install` updates without losing settings.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Alternatives: config in `/usr/share`: lost on every update.
